1
00:00:12,429 --> 00:00:15,765
AS YOU STOOD BY

2
00:00:17,100 --> 00:00:20,228
EUN-SU, HUI-SU AND JIN-YOUNG

3
00:00:25,817 --> 00:00:27,027
Jesus.

4
00:00:32,323 --> 00:00:34,034
I could really use a ride.

5
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:48,840
Where are you headed?

6
00:01:03,980 --> 00:01:05,231
DETECTIVE KANG JU-YEON

7
00:01:16,910 --> 00:01:18,703
I'm driving.
I'll call you back.

8
00:01:20,955 --> 00:01:23,875
DETECTIVE KANG JU-YEON
CALL ENDED

9
00:01:32,258 --> 00:01:34,594
SEOUL SEOCHO POLICE STATION

10
00:02:11,005 --> 00:02:12,966
- Ah!
- Who are you?

11
00:02:17,595 --> 00:02:19,388
Fuck!

12
00:02:19,389 --> 00:02:20,472
Ah!

13
00:02:23,393 --> 00:02:24,769
- Who the hell are you?
- Bitch!

14
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:27,397
I'm not telling you shit.

15
00:02:44,789 --> 00:02:45,707
Ah!

16
00:02:46,291 --> 00:02:47,375
Fuck! Get lost!

17
00:02:47,959 --> 00:02:49,043
Stop!

18
00:02:53,339 --> 00:02:55,508
You know me? How's that?

19
00:02:56,092 --> 00:02:57,135
And you?

20
00:02:57,802 --> 00:02:59,596
How'd you manage to track me down?

21
00:03:00,430 --> 00:03:02,599
Did Jo Eun-su try to recruit you too?

22
00:03:03,850 --> 00:03:04,683
Jo Eun-su?

23
00:03:04,684 --> 00:03:06,268
Shit!

24
00:03:08,479 --> 00:03:11,023
Why are you cuffing me?

25
00:03:13,693 --> 00:03:15,402
I haven't done anything wrong.

26
00:03:15,403 --> 00:03:16,529
Shit.

27
00:03:17,405 --> 00:03:19,615
You can't do this to me! Let me go!

28
00:03:21,117 --> 00:03:22,743
- Shit.
- Let me go, dammit.

29
00:03:22,744 --> 00:03:25,538
You hear me?
Get these fucking things off me.

30
00:03:28,917 --> 00:03:29,918
Jin-pyo?

31
00:03:34,631 --> 00:03:36,591
Why do you have my brother's phone?

32
00:03:37,175 --> 00:03:38,176
I found it.

33
00:03:39,093 --> 00:03:40,552
What, is that a crime now?

34
00:03:45,058 --> 00:03:46,100
Fuck.

35
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:49,479
Hey! Don't! Fuck!

36
00:03:52,690 --> 00:03:53,815
Get off my phone.

37
00:03:53,816 --> 00:03:56,236
I said get off my fucking phone!

38
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:08,539
JO HUI-SU

39
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,125
Hui-su?

40
00:04:11,626 --> 00:04:13,919
JO HUI-SU

41
00:04:18,216 --> 00:04:20,051
How do you know Hui-su?

42
00:04:20,635 --> 00:04:21,886
Why did you call her?

43
00:04:23,012 --> 00:04:24,554
Uncuff me, and we can talk.

44
00:04:24,555 --> 00:04:27,392
Extorting my mother
and blackmailing Hui-su?

45
00:04:28,351 --> 00:04:29,269
Why do that?

46
00:04:32,188 --> 00:04:33,940
Jin-pyo put you up to it?

47
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:40,070
Oh shit, man.

48
00:04:42,532 --> 00:04:43,950
You don't know shit.

49
00:04:45,118 --> 00:04:46,077
Huh?

50
00:04:57,380 --> 00:04:59,756
<i>The caller you are trying
to reach is unavailable.</i>

51
00:04:59,757 --> 00:05:03,094
<i>Are you still at work?
Why aren't you picking up?</i>

52
00:05:11,185 --> 00:05:13,770
<i>If Jang Kang calls today,
just don't pick up.</i>

53
00:05:13,771 --> 00:05:15,398
I'm gonna meet him and settle this.

54
00:05:31,998 --> 00:05:35,001
JO HUI-SU

55
00:05:41,883 --> 00:05:42,717
<i>Hello?</i>

56
00:05:43,217 --> 00:05:44,927
<i>Mr. Jang, this is Hui-su.</i>

57
00:05:45,678 --> 00:05:46,637
<i>Hello?</i>

58
00:06:07,241 --> 00:06:09,369
MR. JIN SO-BAEK

59
00:06:15,458 --> 00:06:16,292
Yes, Mr. Jin?

60
00:06:16,876 --> 00:06:18,920
It's urgent. I need you.

61
00:06:19,420 --> 00:06:21,255
Get to the warehouse as soon as you can.

62
00:06:25,134 --> 00:06:27,095
<i>Eun-su is on her way here too.</i>

63
00:06:28,930 --> 00:06:32,016
Thirty minutes, Detective.
That's the most I can give you.

64
00:07:04,507 --> 00:07:05,591
A tattoo?

65
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:11,389
Why do you have
my brother's phone?

66
00:07:23,818 --> 00:07:25,945
That's not Jin-pyo at the airport at all.

67
00:08:05,443 --> 00:08:07,069
Somebody switched the luggage.

68
00:08:10,448 --> 00:08:11,407
Jesus Christ.

69
00:08:12,992 --> 00:08:14,368
Is he in there?

70
00:08:50,154 --> 00:08:55,534
JO EUN-SU

71
00:08:55,535 --> 00:08:57,577
<i>Oh wow.</i>

72
00:08:57,578 --> 00:08:59,205
<i>Noh Jin-pyo.</i>

73
00:09:00,289 --> 00:09:02,332
<i>- He's here, isn't he?</i>

74
00:09:02,333 --> 00:09:04,377
<i>Huh?</i>

75
00:09:35,032 --> 00:09:36,784
So they were friends?

76
00:09:57,888 --> 00:09:59,098
Idiot.

77
00:10:37,470 --> 00:10:39,555
It was you. Wasn't it?

78
00:10:40,973 --> 00:10:42,016
You did it.

79
00:10:44,810 --> 00:10:46,270
You killed my brother.

80
00:10:52,568 --> 00:10:55,195
Fortunately,
it's just a flesh wound.

81
00:10:55,196 --> 00:10:56,697
It should heal up fine.

82
00:10:58,991 --> 00:11:00,201
So I'll be on my way.

83
00:11:01,077 --> 00:11:02,495
Thank you, Doctor.

84
00:11:14,382 --> 00:11:15,508
I'm sorry.

85
00:11:16,258 --> 00:11:17,759
He could've killed you.

86
00:11:17,760 --> 00:11:20,763
You know how dangerous he is,
and you still went and did that?

87
00:11:23,349 --> 00:11:24,849
I guess I got cocky.

88
00:11:24,850 --> 00:11:27,186
And it almost got you killed!

89
00:11:34,110 --> 00:11:35,528
What if I'd lost you?

90
00:11:36,028 --> 00:11:38,364
After what you did to save me from him.

91
00:11:45,913 --> 00:11:48,082
It wasn't only about helping you though.

92
00:11:52,878 --> 00:11:55,506
There are so many things
I've avoided in my life.

93
00:11:59,051 --> 00:12:02,138
When I was little,
it was all I'd ever known.

94
00:12:02,638 --> 00:12:04,139
Just part of childhood.

95
00:12:04,140 --> 00:12:05,265
And as my dad got older,

96
00:12:05,266 --> 00:12:08,060
I thought he'd calm down
and stop the abuse.

97
00:12:09,437 --> 00:12:12,356
And when I realized
he was still hurting her, I ignored it.

98
00:12:14,275 --> 00:12:17,485
I was afraid I'd lose the life
I'd built here and get sucked back in.

99
00:12:17,486 --> 00:12:19,447
So I pretended not to know.

100
00:12:22,575 --> 00:12:25,744
But with everything that led
to Mrs. Kang killing herself, I realized...

101
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:27,245
DEARLY DEPARTED MS. KANG HUI-YEON

102
00:12:27,246 --> 00:12:29,331
<i>...if I don't break the cycle,</i>

103
00:12:29,999 --> 00:12:31,459
<i>it will never end.</i>

104
00:12:36,046 --> 00:12:37,381
That's why I did it.

105
00:12:39,049 --> 00:12:40,676
It wasn't just for you.

106
00:12:41,218 --> 00:12:43,262
I needed to break it for me too.

107
00:12:45,639 --> 00:12:47,725
You don't have to carry all the weight.

108
00:12:55,065 --> 00:12:56,274
Are you in pain?

109
00:12:56,275 --> 00:12:57,692
Why? Does it look bad?

110
00:12:57,693 --> 00:12:59,527
Not with the bandage.

111
00:12:59,528 --> 00:13:00,488
It's fine.

112
00:13:08,704 --> 00:13:11,957
It's times like these,
you gotta break out the strong stuff.

113
00:13:14,794 --> 00:13:17,338
Steer clear of Jang Kang from now on.

114
00:13:22,718 --> 00:13:23,594
How did you know?

115
00:13:24,345 --> 00:13:26,805
Is there anything
I don't know around here?

116
00:13:41,111 --> 00:13:44,073
I know what you've been up to and that
you're in deeper than you can handle.

117
00:13:48,828 --> 00:13:49,745
Hmm?

118
00:13:55,167 --> 00:13:57,837
I'm surprised you got this far
without getting caught.

119
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:13,476
Those memories will always
come back to haunt you,

120
00:14:13,477 --> 00:14:15,771
no matter how far you try to run.

121
00:15:02,026 --> 00:15:03,109
That happened 20 years ago,

122
00:15:03,110 --> 00:15:05,905
but sometimes I feel like
I'm still covered in blood.

123
00:15:16,957 --> 00:15:20,669
You know, what you two did
is kind of admirable in a way.

124
00:15:25,007 --> 00:15:27,551
I had a chance to see some things
on your husband's phone.

125
00:15:31,347 --> 00:15:33,807
Son of a bitch got exactly
what he deserved.

126
00:15:51,283 --> 00:15:52,575
I'll send Jang back to Shanghai.

127
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:56,246
What?

128
00:15:58,958 --> 00:16:01,877
- It's not your problem though.
- You don't stand a chance against the guy.

129
00:16:02,378 --> 00:16:06,631
Okay? He was a stowaway who survived
the roughest slums in China.

130
00:16:06,632 --> 00:16:08,925
He's cunning, and he even managed
to pull one over on me,

131
00:16:08,926 --> 00:16:11,136
and I'm a tough one to fool.

132
00:16:11,971 --> 00:16:13,721
It's only fitting
that I put him in his place.

133
00:16:13,722 --> 00:16:15,808
He's not only cunning, he's vicious.

134
00:16:16,308 --> 00:16:18,935
He won't go down without a fight,
and you don't back down.

135
00:16:18,936 --> 00:16:21,605
I backed down the first time
you showed up here, didn't I?

136
00:16:24,858 --> 00:16:26,985
You're being overly protective,
and I appreciate it--

137
00:16:26,986 --> 00:16:29,570
Then appreciate it.
Do as I say, and it'll be over.

138
00:16:29,571 --> 00:16:32,241
- This is my fault and my problem to solve.
- Enough.

139
00:16:32,741 --> 00:16:34,284
You're on my payroll.

140
00:16:35,953 --> 00:16:37,830
And your friend could be on it soon.

141
00:16:39,373 --> 00:16:41,959
So just accept the fact
that I'm gonna help you.

142
00:16:46,505 --> 00:16:48,465
Jang Kang was nowhere to be found.

143
00:16:49,216 --> 00:16:50,925
And then there's the other car.

144
00:16:50,926 --> 00:16:52,719
<i>When she took the exit all of a sudden,</i>

145
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,472
<i>I thought maybe
she wasn't tailing us after all.</i>

146
00:16:56,348 --> 00:16:57,808
<i>But then she came back.</i>

147
00:16:58,392 --> 00:17:00,477
<i>She drove right past me on that road.</i>

148
00:17:03,272 --> 00:17:05,107
Try running the plate number.

149
00:17:07,026 --> 00:17:09,361
And send someone to watch
where Jang's staying.

150
00:17:10,112 --> 00:17:10,946
Huh?

151
00:17:11,447 --> 00:17:12,364
Uh-huh.

152
00:17:16,618 --> 00:17:18,078
We found your phone.

153
00:17:18,787 --> 00:17:20,664
That's a relief.

154
00:17:21,582 --> 00:17:22,957
When you were driving last night,

155
00:17:22,958 --> 00:17:25,627
did you happen to notice
anyone following you?

156
00:17:38,891 --> 00:17:40,434
PSYCHOTROPIC DRUG
ZOLPIDEM

157
00:18:13,842 --> 00:18:15,135
Where are we?

158
00:18:17,763 --> 00:18:18,889
Jang Kang.

159
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:24,895
Did you make copies of what you saw
on Jin-pyo's phone? Yes or no.

160
00:18:27,106 --> 00:18:28,190
Ah...

161
00:18:29,316 --> 00:18:31,400
Your brother's missing,
and that's your first question?

162
00:18:31,401 --> 00:18:33,153
Did you make any or not?

163
00:18:43,372 --> 00:18:44,915
I'd start talking if I were you.

164
00:18:45,958 --> 00:18:48,252
I know you murdered that security guard.

165
00:18:51,046 --> 00:18:53,173
No, I didn't.

166
00:18:53,799 --> 00:18:56,051
Noh Jin-pyo did that.

167
00:19:08,272 --> 00:19:10,898
Why'd you do that?

168
00:19:10,899 --> 00:19:12,484
Are there any copies?

169
00:19:15,154 --> 00:19:16,321
No, there aren't.

170
00:19:18,198 --> 00:19:21,118
Good boy. That wasn't so hard, was it?

171
00:20:21,094 --> 00:20:24,640
THE FIRST FEMALE COMMISSIONER GENERAL
NOH JIN-YOUNG!

172
00:20:44,326 --> 00:20:45,243
Jin-young.

173
00:20:45,244 --> 00:20:47,162
Hi, did I wake you?

174
00:20:47,788 --> 00:20:48,789
Jin-pyo.

175
00:20:49,498 --> 00:20:50,707
Do you have news?

176
00:20:58,298 --> 00:20:59,508
I think we're close.

177
00:21:01,843 --> 00:21:03,136
Are you drinking again?

178
00:21:04,388 --> 00:21:06,430
Ah, of course not.

179
00:21:06,431 --> 00:21:09,517
I only finished the few drops
that were left from the last bottle.

180
00:21:09,518 --> 00:21:10,560
Go ahead.

181
00:21:11,061 --> 00:21:12,853
Turn the place upside down.
You won't find any.

182
00:21:12,854 --> 00:21:14,397
I made your last DUI go away.

183
00:21:14,398 --> 00:21:15,816
- Remember?
- I know.

184
00:21:22,072 --> 00:21:23,990
I need to borrow your car for a while.

185
00:21:23,991 --> 00:21:25,784
Mine's got a weird noise going on.

186
00:21:26,285 --> 00:21:28,077
The garage at my place
is under renovation,

187
00:21:28,078 --> 00:21:29,620
so I need to leave it here.

188
00:21:29,621 --> 00:21:32,206
It smells awful
from the scenes I've been working.

189
00:21:32,207 --> 00:21:34,418
So stay out of the garage for now.
All right?

190
00:21:55,147 --> 00:21:57,898
MOVING SELECTED ITEMS TO TRASH

191
00:21:57,899 --> 00:21:58,984
NO PHOTOS OR VIDEOS

192
00:22:08,952 --> 00:22:10,786
{\an8}LICENSE PLATE SEARCH RESULTS

193
00:22:10,787 --> 00:22:14,041
{\an8}LICENSE PLATE: 13M 6925
NAME: NOH JIN-YOUNG

194
00:22:17,252 --> 00:22:18,378
Noh Jin-young.

195
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:31,349
You said your husband's name
is Jin-pyo, right?

196
00:22:31,350 --> 00:22:33,018
And his sister is Jin-young?

197
00:22:33,810 --> 00:22:34,853
How do you know Jin-young?

198
00:22:36,980 --> 00:22:39,023
So the car
that was following me last night...

199
00:22:39,024 --> 00:22:40,317
It was Noh Jin-young's.

200
00:22:41,526 --> 00:22:45,447
And Mr. Ma says he saw this car
when Jang Kang got into yours.

201
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:49,409
Noh Jin-young knew he was there
when she followed you.

202
00:22:50,369 --> 00:22:54,121
I don't see how Jin-young could have known
who Eun-su or Jang Kang were.

203
00:22:54,122 --> 00:22:56,749
She hasn't come over lately,
and we haven't talked either.

204
00:22:56,750 --> 00:22:58,042
But she's a cop.

205
00:22:58,043 --> 00:22:59,294
MA HAE-RYONG

206
00:23:00,379 --> 00:23:01,379
Oh, really?

207
00:23:01,380 --> 00:23:04,925
I think she would have called you first
if she'd known anything about Jang.

208
00:23:05,675 --> 00:23:07,301
But she didn't call me.

209
00:23:07,302 --> 00:23:10,721
And I thought for sure Jang would call me
after what went down yesterday,

210
00:23:10,722 --> 00:23:11,890
but he hasn't called either.

211
00:23:12,974 --> 00:23:16,852
I... kinda panicked and called him
when I couldn't reach you last night.

212
00:23:16,853 --> 00:23:20,232
<i>He answered but hung up
without saying anything.</i>

213
00:23:25,028 --> 00:23:28,990
Given that neither one's gotten in touch,
I'd say she's got him.

214
00:23:32,369 --> 00:23:35,539
I look forward to working with you.
So welcome aboard.

215
00:23:39,251 --> 00:23:40,793
You won't be disappointed.

216
00:23:40,794 --> 00:23:42,253
I trust your skills.

217
00:23:42,254 --> 00:23:46,298
But since this is your first posting here,
I'll give you some valuable advice.

218
00:23:46,299 --> 00:23:47,258
Please.

219
00:23:47,259 --> 00:23:48,676
Your friends and family,

220
00:23:48,677 --> 00:23:51,054
you better watch them like a hawk
if you wanna stay.

221
00:23:51,555 --> 00:23:53,305
No matter how capable you are,

222
00:23:53,306 --> 00:23:55,558
if their behavior
tarnishes your reputation,

223
00:23:55,559 --> 00:23:57,269
your days here are over.

224
00:23:58,937 --> 00:24:00,397
I'll make sure to do that.

225
00:24:03,442 --> 00:24:08,362
OFFICE OF THE PRESIDENT
OF THE REPUBLIC OF KOREA

226
00:24:09,906 --> 00:24:11,324
Jin-pyo's already dead.

227
00:24:12,200 --> 00:24:14,577
There's nothing I can do
to change that math.

228
00:24:19,875 --> 00:24:23,170
But maybe I can rewrite

229
00:24:24,379 --> 00:24:25,672
the equation.

230
00:24:33,388 --> 00:24:34,514
<i>15th floor.</i>

231
00:24:44,232 --> 00:24:45,233
Eun-su?

232
00:24:47,027 --> 00:24:48,527
Sounds like you were expecting someone.

233
00:24:48,528 --> 00:24:52,407
Uh, just one of my neighbors
who left her colander here.

234
00:25:00,790 --> 00:25:01,791
Eun-su.

235
00:25:10,133 --> 00:25:11,134
Eun-su?

236
00:25:16,890 --> 00:25:18,934
Sorry. I thought you were someone else.

237
00:25:19,601 --> 00:25:21,186
LEE HYEON-JI

238
00:25:58,598 --> 00:26:00,350
When did this blood get here?

239
00:27:17,302 --> 00:27:18,637
Welcome to Lavie.

240
00:27:21,514 --> 00:27:24,726
Oh, the most doting husband
with excellent taste.

241
00:27:26,394 --> 00:27:28,438
Would you testify to that under oath?

242
00:27:29,189 --> 00:27:30,023
Sorry?

243
00:27:35,195 --> 00:27:38,073
Could I get the new catalogue
for the spring collection, please?

244
00:27:41,284 --> 00:27:43,994
Getting your wife
expensive jewelry doesn't necessarily mean

245
00:27:43,995 --> 00:27:45,080
you love her.

246
00:27:48,124 --> 00:27:50,919
It could just be a matter
of trying to buy forgiveness.

247
00:28:08,353 --> 00:28:10,188
Huh? Go ahead.

248
00:28:15,944 --> 00:28:19,114
<i>It looks like Jin-young knows
about Jang Kang and her brother.</i>

249
00:29:06,161 --> 00:29:08,328
MOTHER

250
00:29:08,329 --> 00:29:11,331
Our specials today
are white ragù and truffle paccheri.

251
00:29:11,332 --> 00:29:12,792
Mm-hmm.

252
00:29:13,877 --> 00:29:17,171
My daughter-in-law will be happy.
Those are her two favorites.

253
00:29:17,172 --> 00:29:18,839
We'll have one of each, please.

254
00:29:18,840 --> 00:29:20,008
Of course.

255
00:29:27,056 --> 00:29:28,141
How are you?

256
00:29:31,144 --> 00:29:32,145
Jin-pyo.

257
00:29:33,229 --> 00:29:34,647
He's back, I guess.

258
00:29:35,398 --> 00:29:36,316
What?

259
00:29:37,859 --> 00:29:40,195
Jin-pyo... has returned.

260
00:29:49,537 --> 00:29:50,788
Is he at work?

261
00:29:52,957 --> 00:29:53,874
You knew?

262
00:29:53,875 --> 00:29:56,544
Weren't you going to tell me
about my son's return?

263
00:29:59,464 --> 00:30:02,217
You knew... what he was doing?

264
00:30:04,052 --> 00:30:06,930
All these years I suffered,
and you never brought it up.

265
00:30:07,722 --> 00:30:11,017
- And now you acknowledge it so casually?
- I don't have time for your nonsense.

266
00:30:12,018 --> 00:30:14,895
If you're going to manipulate Jin-pyo
into begging me for money

267
00:30:14,896 --> 00:30:16,980
dressed like a vagrant again,
set him free.

268
00:30:16,981 --> 00:30:18,525
I'll care for my son.

269
00:30:46,845 --> 00:30:49,556
<i>Noh Jin-young knew he was there
when she followed you.</i>

270
00:30:54,561 --> 00:30:55,770
Hi, how are you?

271
00:30:59,482 --> 00:31:01,067
We really need to talk.

272
00:31:04,654 --> 00:31:06,196
Why didn't you call first?

273
00:31:06,197 --> 00:31:08,199
You were caught on a dashcam.
You know that?

274
00:31:10,618 --> 00:31:11,661
What?

275
00:31:14,289 --> 00:31:16,708
I saw footage of you on someone's dashcam.

276
00:31:17,208 --> 00:31:19,376
From the time
the security guard was murdered.

277
00:31:19,377 --> 00:31:21,504
A resident drove past the scene.

278
00:31:25,174 --> 00:31:27,217
I had forgotten something
in the car that day.

279
00:31:27,218 --> 00:31:29,846
Maybe, but you're not the only one
in the footage.

280
00:31:30,346 --> 00:31:32,640
It appears my brother

281
00:31:33,308 --> 00:31:34,726
was down there too.

282
00:31:41,357 --> 00:31:42,567
He's still gone.

283
00:31:45,737 --> 00:31:47,113
So he wasn't there.

284
00:31:47,780 --> 00:31:49,073
It'd be impossible.

285
00:31:50,867 --> 00:31:54,621
But then again, Mom has started saying
impossible things too.

286
00:31:55,330 --> 00:31:58,458
She'll tell me she saw Jin-pyo,
and then take it back.

287
00:31:59,042 --> 00:32:01,920
"Never mind.
Just wishful thinking," she says.

288
00:32:03,212 --> 00:32:04,339
So I thought

289
00:32:06,007 --> 00:32:07,383
maybe I should ask you.

290
00:32:12,055 --> 00:32:12,889
About what?

291
00:32:16,601 --> 00:32:17,852
Hui-su.

292
00:32:20,521 --> 00:32:21,940
Where the fuck is he?

293
00:32:25,568 --> 00:32:28,863
Jin-pyo is... in Shanghai, last I heard.

294
00:32:34,035 --> 00:32:36,328
Yeah. That's right.

295
00:32:36,329 --> 00:32:38,164
He took off on you.

296
00:32:39,624 --> 00:32:41,709
But he'll be back eventually.

297
00:32:44,796 --> 00:32:46,172
You know that, right?

298
00:32:49,258 --> 00:32:50,093
Yes.

299
00:33:12,198 --> 00:33:13,116
When?

300
00:33:14,909 --> 00:33:16,744
She's driving her mother's car now?

301
00:33:21,749 --> 00:33:24,377
And we're sure
she didn't hand him over to the police?

302
00:33:26,045 --> 00:33:27,046
Mm-hmm.

303
00:33:27,672 --> 00:33:29,340
Go to Ko Jeong-suk's for now.

304
00:33:30,133 --> 00:33:31,134
Yes.

305
00:33:32,510 --> 00:33:33,678
Jin-young's mother.

306
00:33:34,178 --> 00:33:35,972
- That's Ko Jeong-suk?
- Yeah, you know her?

307
00:33:37,348 --> 00:33:39,600
Jin-young needs a clean family record.

308
00:33:40,435 --> 00:33:42,519
She wants a position
on the Presidential detail,

309
00:33:42,520 --> 00:33:44,564
so that would explain
why she's gone quiet.

310
00:33:45,732 --> 00:33:48,316
Wow, another layer.

311
00:33:51,487 --> 00:33:52,779
Until we know...

312
00:33:52,780 --> 00:33:56,409
You think...
she could have hidden Jang in her car?

313
00:34:03,833 --> 00:34:06,043
We'll wait for the call. Okay?

314
00:34:06,044 --> 00:34:07,295
Let's just wait.

315
00:35:03,226 --> 00:35:04,268
This is she.

316
00:35:05,478 --> 00:35:08,314
Oh, the Lavie department store?

317
00:35:09,315 --> 00:35:10,148
Yes.

318
00:35:10,149 --> 00:35:11,525
They're beautiful.

319
00:35:11,526 --> 00:35:13,528
- Please have a seat.
- Thank you.

320
00:35:14,403 --> 00:35:16,613
First, I apologize for the short notice,

321
00:35:16,614 --> 00:35:20,075
but it would be such an honor
to have you speak at our VVIP event.

322
00:35:20,076 --> 00:35:23,453
I really appreciate your making the time
to see me, Mrs. Ko.

323
00:35:23,454 --> 00:35:25,080
When my children were little,

324
00:35:25,081 --> 00:35:28,334
there wasn't a single day
we didn't have fresh flowers in the house.

325
00:35:28,835 --> 00:35:32,255
On the priority list,
flowers came before food.

326
00:35:32,755 --> 00:35:37,384
I truly believe that both my children
grew up to be gentle and kindhearted

327
00:35:37,385 --> 00:35:41,139
because they were always surrounded
by the peaceful beauty of flowers.

328
00:35:41,806 --> 00:35:43,014
I see.

329
00:35:43,015 --> 00:35:45,643
So, these VVIP customers...

330
00:35:46,144 --> 00:35:47,937
Is there a theme for the day?

331
00:35:51,274 --> 00:35:52,274
I feel so rude,

332
00:35:52,275 --> 00:35:54,526
but would you please
excuse me for a moment?

333
00:35:54,527 --> 00:35:55,778
I really need to take this.

334
00:35:56,487 --> 00:35:57,613
Of course.

335
00:35:59,157 --> 00:36:01,909
Yes, I'm at a meeting
with our future guest speaker.

336
00:36:34,525 --> 00:36:36,110
Jang Kang.

337
00:36:37,069 --> 00:36:39,238
This is Eun-su. I'll get you out of there.

338
00:36:59,008 --> 00:36:59,842
Come on.

339
00:37:00,801 --> 00:37:02,929
Jang Kang!

340
00:37:33,876 --> 00:37:35,711
Disable it before they send someone.

341
00:37:43,135 --> 00:37:44,512
JO EUN-SU

342
00:38:08,244 --> 00:38:10,371
There's something I think
I should tell you.

343
00:38:13,165 --> 00:38:15,835
Hui-su thought the security guard
was spying on her.

344
00:38:16,669 --> 00:38:19,255
She wanted to file a complaint,
but I convinced her not to.

345
00:38:21,132 --> 00:38:23,884
But apparently, she threatened him anyway
without proof.

346
00:38:25,970 --> 00:38:29,682
What kind of bothers me
is that man's the one who got killed.

347
00:38:30,182 --> 00:38:33,351
Caught my attention,
which is why I rushed over there that day.

348
00:38:33,352 --> 00:38:34,520
Oh, right.

349
00:38:37,773 --> 00:38:39,190
We questioned a couple at the scene.

350
00:38:39,191 --> 00:38:41,192
They left the garage
around the time of the crime,

351
00:38:41,193 --> 00:38:44,571
and luckily, your sister-in-law
was cleared by their statement.

352
00:38:44,572 --> 00:38:45,573
Hmm.

353
00:38:47,283 --> 00:38:48,409
That is lucky.

354
00:38:50,119 --> 00:38:53,079
Oh. I wanted to thank you.

355
00:38:53,080 --> 00:38:56,542
For not mentioning her visit,
that day she came in.

356
00:38:57,835 --> 00:38:58,753
Sorry?

357
00:39:00,546 --> 00:39:03,089
Ah. You don't have to thank me for that.

358
00:39:05,718 --> 00:39:07,636
She has serious issues.

359
00:39:08,137 --> 00:39:10,013
She, uh,

360
00:39:10,014 --> 00:39:13,184
hurts herself and pretends
that someone else did it.

361
00:39:14,435 --> 00:39:16,311
She's going to try
to pin my brother for abuse,

362
00:39:16,312 --> 00:39:18,856
but she saw me and ran off.

363
00:39:23,944 --> 00:39:25,779
You know what?
I've told you too much already.

364
00:39:25,780 --> 00:39:27,656
I took up your whole break.

365
00:39:28,407 --> 00:39:30,492
- I'll buy you a drink next time.
- Or coffee's fine too.

366
00:39:30,493 --> 00:39:31,911
- Yeah.
- At your service.

367
00:39:39,418 --> 00:39:40,252
Yeah?

368
00:39:44,423 --> 00:39:45,508
When was this?

369
00:39:53,349 --> 00:39:54,183
Damn it.

370
00:39:56,727 --> 00:39:58,604
Shit.

371
00:40:06,362 --> 00:40:07,738
- Jin-young.
- Mom.

372
00:40:08,531 --> 00:40:11,908
- You didn't call the police, did you?
- Of course not. I waited for you.

373
00:40:11,909 --> 00:40:14,994
- But you should check what's missing.
- We need to check the cameras first.

374
00:40:14,995 --> 00:40:17,080
No, it was a woman who came here.

375
00:40:17,081 --> 00:40:20,583
She... pretended she works at
that fancy department store.

376
00:40:20,584 --> 00:40:22,919
She said she wanted me to give a speech.

377
00:40:22,920 --> 00:40:24,588
- But it was a trick.
- Department store?

378
00:40:25,172 --> 00:40:26,298
Do you mean Lavie?

379
00:40:26,799 --> 00:40:27,633
Yes.

380
00:40:37,893 --> 00:40:39,520
What the hell is wrong with you?

381
00:40:40,813 --> 00:40:42,982
I had to do something.
Who knows what she would've done--

382
00:40:46,277 --> 00:40:47,945
I told you I would take care of it.

383
00:40:49,697 --> 00:40:51,448
Where were you planning to go?

384
00:40:51,449 --> 00:40:53,700
Were you just gonna keep driving
till you figured it out?

385
00:40:53,701 --> 00:40:55,453
How long were you gonna drive?

386
00:40:56,871 --> 00:40:59,623
I assume you have some kind of plan,
since you took him?

387
00:41:07,131 --> 00:41:09,592
You trying to get hurt?
'Cause that's how you're acting!

388
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:30,612
JINGANG CHINESE MARKET

389
00:41:51,050 --> 00:41:53,677
Jang Kang is going back
on the first boat I can find.

390
00:41:54,220 --> 00:41:55,137
Okay.

391
00:41:55,763 --> 00:41:57,223
Noh Jin-pyo as well.

392
00:41:58,641 --> 00:41:59,517
Huh?

393
00:42:00,100 --> 00:42:01,184
Mr. Jin?

394
00:42:01,185 --> 00:42:02,185
Noh Jin-pyo died.

395
00:42:02,186 --> 00:42:04,062
He left for Shanghai
a month and a half ago,

396
00:42:04,063 --> 00:42:06,315
and things went terribly wrong.

397
00:42:10,152 --> 00:42:13,029
If you're doing all of this
because of what you said

398
00:42:13,030 --> 00:42:16,282
when we were talking over soup,
you really don't have to at all

399
00:42:16,283 --> 00:42:19,661
'cause I was so completely stressed out,
I don't remember a thing you said.

400
00:42:19,662 --> 00:42:22,080
If Jin-pyo's still in Korea, then what?

401
00:42:25,376 --> 00:42:27,503
If you have a better solution,
I'm listening.

402
00:42:44,186 --> 00:42:48,314
<i>Gangneung Chodang
Police report, 1999.</i>

403
00:42:48,315 --> 00:42:49,400
<i>Ring a bell?</i>

404
00:42:51,902 --> 00:42:53,112
I got it here.

405
00:42:53,779 --> 00:42:56,532
112 EMERGENCY CALL INCIDENT REPORT

406
00:43:00,953 --> 00:43:02,580
<i>You were eight at the time.</i>

407
00:43:08,752 --> 00:43:10,379
Can't believe this.

408
00:43:10,963 --> 00:43:14,799
All I did was turn the volume up
to watch the wrestling on television.

409
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:16,135
Is that a crime now?

410
00:43:18,053 --> 00:43:20,598
I bumped my face
cleaning the bathroom earlier.

411
00:43:21,265 --> 00:43:24,058
We'll need to talk to
anyone else who's in the house.

412
00:43:24,059 --> 00:43:25,853
It's okay. You can come out.

413
00:43:27,104 --> 00:43:27,937
Hi.

414
00:43:29,690 --> 00:43:33,986
Can you tell us if you heard anything
like fighting or yelling earlier?

415
00:43:35,279 --> 00:43:38,698
I... I fell asleep. I didn't hear anything.

416
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:43,286
I was in the closet
with my brother.

417
00:43:43,287 --> 00:43:45,705
We were there playing hide and seek.

418
00:43:49,752 --> 00:43:51,919
<i>You turned a blind eye
to your own family.</i>

419
00:43:51,920 --> 00:43:55,257
So why are you all of a sudden
meddling in someone else's?

420
00:43:55,924 --> 00:43:59,887
Is this some kind of attempt
at alleviating your conscience?

421
00:44:01,388 --> 00:44:03,641
If you thought
you'd come out of this a hero,

422
00:44:04,141 --> 00:44:05,475
you thought wrong.

423
00:44:05,476 --> 00:44:07,561
The only thing this is gonna get you...

424
00:44:09,855 --> 00:44:11,065
is charged with murder.

425
00:44:14,276 --> 00:44:16,069
We'll find out soon enough, won't we?

426
00:44:16,070 --> 00:44:18,655
I don't need Jang Kang to put you two--

427
00:44:24,078 --> 00:44:26,287
MR. JIN SO-BAEK

428
00:44:26,288 --> 00:44:28,373
<i>Your call cannot be completed.</i>

429
00:44:28,374 --> 00:44:30,000
MR. JIN SO-BAEK

430
00:44:36,882 --> 00:44:37,925
Mr. Jin.

431
00:44:38,801 --> 00:44:40,803
You're right.
Jin-pyo needs to die in China.

432
00:44:54,441 --> 00:44:55,984
Just shut up!

433
00:44:58,987 --> 00:45:01,365
Where's Jo Eun-su? Huh?

434
00:45:01,865 --> 00:45:04,325
Get her in here!

435
00:45:04,326 --> 00:45:05,703
Go get her!

436
00:45:06,245 --> 00:45:07,413
I said shut it.

437
00:45:07,913 --> 00:45:10,415
You'll be on the first boat
out of here tonight.

438
00:45:10,416 --> 00:45:11,875
You don't give orders here!

439
00:45:37,943 --> 00:45:39,570
Jo Hui-su.

440
00:45:41,864 --> 00:45:45,199
She had been secretly siphoning off
her husband's money,

441
00:45:45,200 --> 00:45:46,744
and when he found out,

442
00:45:47,244 --> 00:45:50,873
she faked injuries to make it look like
he was abusing her.

443
00:45:51,498 --> 00:45:54,251
Then she used it to blackmail him.

444
00:45:55,753 --> 00:45:59,005
But that wasn't enough
to satisfy her greed.

445
00:45:59,006 --> 00:46:03,426
So she recruited her best friend,
Jo Eun-su, to kill him.

446
00:46:08,474 --> 00:46:11,476
Then they pretended
a loving husband had just run off.

447
00:46:25,616 --> 00:46:26,784
Then buried him.

448
00:46:32,831 --> 00:46:34,500
You're driving me nuts.

449
00:46:42,841 --> 00:46:45,259
I need water, man! Please!

450
00:47:04,321 --> 00:47:05,655
Sit up.

451
00:47:05,656 --> 00:47:07,157
Take it easy.

452
00:47:11,036 --> 00:47:12,955
Bastard!

453
00:47:14,289 --> 00:47:15,790
When I get back,

454
00:47:15,791 --> 00:47:19,169
first thing on my list is gonna be
to hunt down your entire family

455
00:47:19,962 --> 00:47:22,004
and cut 'em into pieces.

456
00:47:22,005 --> 00:47:24,423
After I tell them
it's because of you. Fuck!

457
00:47:41,900 --> 00:47:43,151
Pull over.

458
00:47:54,788 --> 00:47:55,664
So, uh...

459
00:47:59,209 --> 00:48:00,210
good luck

460
00:48:00,711 --> 00:48:01,795
and all that.

461
00:48:25,402 --> 00:48:26,987
Crazy bitch.

462
00:48:35,454 --> 00:48:38,373
I can take you to where he's buried.

463
00:48:42,002 --> 00:48:44,504
Your sister-in-law
and her friend won't say shit.

464
00:48:45,714 --> 00:48:47,466
So we dig up your brother.

465
00:48:49,343 --> 00:48:51,094
And take 'em for all they've got.

466
00:48:58,143 --> 00:48:59,394
How much do you want?

467
00:48:59,978 --> 00:49:01,270
Three billion.

468
00:49:04,942 --> 00:49:06,777
That's 100 million off for you.

469
00:49:08,111 --> 00:49:09,863
Mm. Wait.

470
00:49:10,405 --> 00:49:11,323
Come on.

471
00:49:11,949 --> 00:49:12,783
Come on.

472
00:49:13,325 --> 00:49:14,158
Get in.

473
00:49:17,663 --> 00:49:19,665
Well, fuck me.

474
00:49:20,457 --> 00:49:21,375
Deal?

475
00:49:25,754 --> 00:49:27,464
You really need to do this?

476
00:49:28,840 --> 00:49:30,467
I hired the asshole.

477
00:49:36,848 --> 00:49:37,932
WI CHUN-GIL

478
00:49:46,483 --> 00:49:48,234
- Excellent work today.
- Thank you, ma'am.

479
00:49:48,235 --> 00:49:49,319
- Good night.
- Good night.

480
00:49:58,286 --> 00:49:59,121
Hi.

481
00:49:59,621 --> 00:50:01,957
I'm heading over now.
Should I bring anything?

482
00:50:02,457 --> 00:50:04,960
Oh, before I forget,
you need to find your passport.

483
00:50:06,753 --> 00:50:07,712
Mm-hmm.

484
00:50:07,713 --> 00:50:10,090
He says we should have them on us
just in case.

485
00:50:10,674 --> 00:50:11,883
Another thing.

486
00:50:15,554 --> 00:50:17,139
No, forget it. It can wait.

487
00:50:18,807 --> 00:50:19,725
Mm-hmm.

488
00:50:27,858 --> 00:50:29,151
Did you find a ship?

489
00:50:40,203 --> 00:50:41,203
MR. JIN SO-BAEK

490
00:50:42,831 --> 00:50:46,168
Go to the mah-jongg club with Hui-su.
Make sure you lock the door.

491
00:50:47,878 --> 00:50:49,462
- Turn it around.
- Yes, sir.

492
00:51:29,878 --> 00:51:32,047
Son of bitch. Where is he?

493
00:51:33,882 --> 00:51:36,550
Fuck! Piece of shit!

494
00:51:57,155 --> 00:51:58,448
Look!

495
00:52:03,620 --> 00:52:04,704
I told you!

496
00:52:22,389 --> 00:52:23,557
Holy shit.

497
00:52:24,516 --> 00:52:26,184
Is that a fucking deer head?

498
00:52:47,455 --> 00:52:48,873
This is the spot.

499
00:52:48,874 --> 00:52:49,833
I know it.

500
00:52:50,542 --> 00:52:51,585
And these are

501
00:52:53,336 --> 00:52:54,504
the same trees.

502
00:52:58,383 --> 00:53:00,468
Are you just gonna stand there? Fuck!

503
00:53:02,637 --> 00:53:04,680
You need to help me dig this fucker up!

504
00:53:04,681 --> 00:53:06,932
Oh shit. Fuck!

505
00:53:29,372 --> 00:53:30,832
Looks like you

506
00:53:32,167 --> 00:53:33,459
did find the spot.

507
00:53:59,152 --> 00:54:01,111
MEDICAL CERTIFICATE OF BODILY HARM

508
00:54:05,867 --> 00:54:08,328
MEDICAL CERTIFICATE OF BODILY HARM
JO HUI-SU

509
00:54:14,334 --> 00:54:16,711
It was a clear case of domestic violence.

510
00:54:18,004 --> 00:54:20,548
I encouraged her to report the abuse.

511
00:54:21,800 --> 00:54:22,926
And you're sure about that?

512
00:54:23,551 --> 00:54:24,594
Yes.

513
00:54:54,541 --> 00:54:56,084
Ah, hello, ma'am.

514
00:54:57,836 --> 00:55:00,964
I'm not sure you remember,
but we met once. I'm Officer Choi.

515
00:55:03,800 --> 00:55:04,926
Officer Choi.

516
00:55:05,510 --> 00:55:08,888
I'm here to get some more information
about the security guard's murder.

517
00:55:11,057 --> 00:55:12,141
I see.

518
00:55:12,142 --> 00:55:13,977
And I brought this.

519
00:55:16,813 --> 00:55:18,814
MEDICAL CERTIFICATE OF BODILY HARM

520
00:55:24,612 --> 00:55:26,281
<i>- The door is open.</i>

521
00:55:32,662 --> 00:55:37,167
I... should've paid more attention
when you were at the station

522
00:55:37,667 --> 00:55:39,127
and offered you more help.

523
00:55:40,086 --> 00:55:41,338
It was my mistake.

524
00:55:46,593 --> 00:55:47,469
Uh...

525
00:55:50,513 --> 00:55:52,098
Maybe you want some water?

526
00:56:06,321 --> 00:56:07,864
- Here you are.
- Oh.

527
00:56:08,948 --> 00:56:09,949
Thank you, ma'am.

528
00:56:11,201 --> 00:56:14,829
On the night in question,
you were picked up on someone's dashcam.

529
00:56:15,330 --> 00:56:17,165
Pretty near the scene of the murder.

530
00:56:21,336 --> 00:56:22,461
You were seen in the garage,

531
00:56:22,462 --> 00:56:24,506
and I would like to know
what you were doing there.

532
00:56:26,341 --> 00:56:28,343
There was something I needed in the car.

533
00:56:29,469 --> 00:56:34,015
It says your car wasn't in the garage,
but in the outdoor near your building.

534
00:56:34,599 --> 00:56:35,975
Where you usually park.

535
00:56:37,727 --> 00:56:40,813
Um, I meant to say I was getting something
from my husband's car.

536
00:56:40,814 --> 00:56:42,524
He always parks it down there.

537
00:56:43,108 --> 00:56:45,567
He worries it'll get scratched
if it's outside.

538
00:56:45,568 --> 00:56:46,736
Ah.

539
00:56:49,781 --> 00:56:50,989
That's it for me.

540
00:56:50,990 --> 00:56:53,158
If you think of anything, give me a call.

541
00:56:53,159 --> 00:56:55,202
And I'll be back
if I need more information.

542
00:56:55,203 --> 00:56:56,537
All right. Thank you.

543
00:56:59,457 --> 00:57:00,875
Uh, one last thing.

544
00:57:03,962 --> 00:57:05,588
Do you need help with anything?

545
00:57:09,968 --> 00:57:10,927
Uh, no.

546
00:57:11,886 --> 00:57:13,555
And my husband's traveling.

547
00:57:17,142 --> 00:57:18,560
It's nice of you to ask.

548
00:57:24,732 --> 00:57:27,985
SENTINEL STUDIO APARTMENT

549
00:58:03,563 --> 00:58:04,647
JIN-YOUNG

550
00:58:13,198 --> 00:58:14,198
Oh my God.

551
00:58:17,577 --> 00:58:19,329
Eun-su.

552
00:58:20,872 --> 00:58:23,166
JIN-YOUNG

553
00:58:35,678 --> 00:58:37,679
<i>Call Eun-su, and she dies.</i>

554
00:58:37,680 --> 00:58:40,642
<i>Same goes for your dear mom
at the nursing home.</i>

555
00:58:58,826 --> 00:59:01,703
Eun-su had nothing to do with this.
It was all my doing.

556
00:59:01,704 --> 00:59:05,124
And my mom doesn't...
Just leave my mom alone. I beg you.

557
00:59:06,167 --> 00:59:08,919
Do you really think I believe
your best friend wasn't involved?

558
00:59:08,920 --> 00:59:12,590
She went to my mother's house
and kidnapped Jang Kang from my car.

559
00:59:13,258 --> 00:59:15,260
What?

560
00:59:15,969 --> 00:59:17,177
Where is she now?

561
00:59:17,178 --> 00:59:20,890
- Tell me what you did to Eun-su!
- I didn't do anything to her.

562
00:59:21,474 --> 00:59:23,308
But I found Jang in a terrible state

563
00:59:23,309 --> 00:59:25,770
and rescued him
after she left him for dead.

564
00:59:28,231 --> 00:59:29,440
I don't believe you.

565
00:59:30,316 --> 00:59:31,567
Why should I even listen to you?

566
00:59:31,568 --> 00:59:34,195
<i>Think of everything
your friend has done for you.</i>

567
00:59:38,616 --> 00:59:40,159
<i>Jo Eun-su</i>

568
00:59:41,536 --> 00:59:43,329
<i>is unstable.</i>

569
00:59:45,498 --> 00:59:47,417
<i>Who knows what she'll do next?</i>

570
00:59:48,418 --> 00:59:50,712
<i>But she'll stop at nothing to help you.</i>

571
00:59:56,593 --> 00:59:57,884
<i>Am I wrong?</i>

572
01:00:01,055 --> 01:00:02,556
Kill yourself.

573
01:00:02,557 --> 01:00:03,683
Tonight.

574
01:00:10,231 --> 01:00:12,357
Then I'll let your accomplice
off the hook.

575
01:00:12,358 --> 01:00:13,776
And leave your mom alone too.

576
01:00:15,528 --> 01:00:18,196
<i>I finally got the job
with the president's office.</i>

577
01:00:18,197 --> 01:00:20,491
<i>- Do you think I want this to blow up?</i>

578
01:00:21,117 --> 01:00:25,371
It's not like my dead brother
will be back to testify, will he?

579
01:00:30,126 --> 01:00:32,086
But one of you has to pay, right?

580
01:00:35,048 --> 01:00:38,426
<i>Now that his body's been found,
the clock is ticking.</i>

581
01:00:39,135 --> 01:00:40,178
<i>Stop crying.</i>

582
01:00:42,597 --> 01:00:44,307
It'll be over real soon.

583
01:00:46,267 --> 01:00:47,727
Just go quietly.

584
01:01:58,548 --> 01:02:01,718
EUN-SU

585
01:02:12,186 --> 01:02:13,396
Hey, Eun-su.

586
01:02:25,950 --> 01:02:27,284
What happened to your forehead?

587
01:02:27,285 --> 01:02:29,328
Oh, I tripped on the desk.

588
01:02:31,831 --> 01:02:33,249
I actually did.

589
01:02:33,791 --> 01:02:36,001
Making piles of all the things to sell.

590
01:02:36,002 --> 01:02:37,503
Well, be more careful.

591
01:02:38,004 --> 01:02:39,337
Next stop, mah-jongg club.

592
01:02:39,338 --> 01:02:41,507
Mm. Let's go.

593
01:03:19,879 --> 01:03:22,632
- Hui-su.
- I've been on edge, and I'm too stressed.

594
01:03:23,591 --> 01:03:25,509
The clattering takes all of it away.

595
01:03:27,011 --> 01:03:28,221
You should try.

596
01:03:29,555 --> 01:03:30,431
Hmm.

597
01:03:34,644 --> 01:03:36,812
Just like Mr. Jin.

598
01:03:36,813 --> 01:03:37,814
Clatter, clatter.

599
01:03:38,397 --> 01:03:39,231
Listen--

600
01:03:39,232 --> 01:03:42,025
Do you remember
when we'd go to the Jungang Market

601
01:03:42,026 --> 01:03:44,654
to get candied chicken
instead of going to study hall?

602
01:03:47,240 --> 01:03:48,532
Masan granny's chicken?

603
01:03:48,533 --> 01:03:51,786
Oh! Ah, such good memories.
I'm craving it right now.

604
01:03:52,328 --> 01:03:54,663
You think it still exists? She was old.

605
01:03:54,664 --> 01:03:58,500
Maybe. Or somebody else
may have taken it over.

606
01:03:58,501 --> 01:04:00,628
Now I'm curious.

607
01:04:02,964 --> 01:04:05,090
She still has it.

608
01:04:08,135 --> 01:04:10,054
There's even a picture of her. Look.

609
01:04:14,267 --> 01:04:16,268
Almost all five-star reviews.

610
01:04:16,269 --> 01:04:18,938
That's so cool.
We'll go there soon. My treat.

611
01:04:20,690 --> 01:04:21,523
Okay.

612
01:04:21,524 --> 01:04:24,694
You know, this made me hungry.
You want some soup?

613
01:04:31,784 --> 01:04:34,245
So you put on lipstick before you eat now?

614
01:04:35,329 --> 01:04:36,830
Just like the old days.

615
01:04:42,753 --> 01:04:44,588
I just need to go to the bathroom.

616
01:04:44,589 --> 01:04:46,883
Don't take too long,
or they're gonna get soggy.

617
01:04:54,056 --> 01:04:55,349
Thank you, Eun-su.

618
01:04:58,728 --> 01:05:00,021
Hurry up. I'm starving.

619
01:05:01,397 --> 01:05:02,315
Mm.

620
01:05:43,940 --> 01:05:46,733
EUN-SU

621
01:06:26,899 --> 01:06:28,984
MOM
I'M SORRY TO LEAVE YOU ALL ALONE

622
01:06:28,985 --> 01:06:31,861
I COMMITTED AN UNFORGIVABLE SIN
I KILLED JIN-PYO

623
01:06:31,862 --> 01:06:32,905
EUN-SU

